From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ScarlettMac <scarlettmac@local>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 15:40:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 04/15] shader: translate tiled cascade shadows exactly on
 wave32 (port of Belobug PR #82)

Upstream after our pin (bf99e72) has no early-out/skip prepass: 58 compute
shaders are still refused in runs/20261126-152702-up720.log, 35 of them
'a lane mask read as data' and 7 'a wave reduction over both 32-lane
halves'. Added ir::without_early_outs and ir::without_skips (deep follows
parked scalars through joins) from Belobug 0cb13721, including the
far-jump form (s_cbranch_execnz over s_getpc/s_add/s_setpc to the end).
The SSA numbering build() did is factored out as ir::rename (upstream has
no vgprs field on Program any more, so rename takes only the blocks and
wave64).

A refused wave64 compute program on a 32-lane host is now retried with
those forms in turn before giving up (Belobug's retry ladder). Default
translations are unchanged.

Tests (host): the far early-out is left out while work in the jump or at
the target keeps it; a skip whose parked scalar passes an inner branch
unchanged needs the deep form, and one that changes it is kept.
